{"duration_api_ms":285918,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a3bd3be4-a343-4f3e-b01a-e13b6c5e23fb","total_cost_usd":0.318668,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12381,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26914,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20253},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12381,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":26914,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12381},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":26914,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12381,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.318668,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":20253,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 16 feasible designs sit in a narrow cluster: D 2.9-3.35 m, cone 55-70 deg, bluntness 0.5-1.15, gamma -3.0 to -3.9. C-11dcf14fd72e is the only feasible non-dominated point (287250 W/m2, 393.73 K). The hypervolume is about 0.885*0.375 = 0.332, so it is set entirely by that one point. With a 2.5e6 W/m2 reference against a 450 K one, 1 K of bondline temperature is worth roughly 40,000 W/m2 of peak flux. I should therefore push bondline temperature down first, then flux. Three limits bind: max_g (12 g), heatshield mass fraction (large D), and a geometry-validity boundary.\",\"evidence\":[\"Mass fraction: 1 - margin divided by D^2 is nearly constant at 0.0877-0.0889 (C-11dcf14fd72e 0.0877, C-4f7f664531cd 0.0874, C-14caae5709dc 0.0889). It falls slightly with higher bluntness and cone angle. The mass limit is therefore D of about 3.37-3.38 m at b >= 1.15 and cone 70.\",\"max_g: at gamma -3.5 it is 11.87 for D >= 3.25 (C-11dcf14fd72e, C-a687c9db7052, C-deeb5fd5f24a) and 11.77 for D 3.1 (C-cb5b9b5d5a6b). The slope is about 1.7 g/deg (C-dc1d6416cb31 to C-22c8ef75dedb to C-0be4678d643c). Gamma of about -3.57 is therefore the g limit at D 3.35.\",\"Gamma trade: C-dc1d6416cb31 (gamma -3.0) vs C-e964c99bacf1 (gamma -3.4) at the same b, cone and D shows +11100 W/m2 and -4.56 K for 0.4 deg steeper. A steeper gamma is the cheapest way to lower bondline temperature.\",\"Bluntness at D 3.1, cone 70: C-cb5b9b5d5a6b (b 1.1) 315290 W/m2, 397.73 K; C-4f7f664531cd (b 1.15) 312530 W/m2, 397.39 K. Lower b is worse: C-6e14665f4a23 (b 0.7) 402.47 K and C-6c22d4ab2deb (b 0.5) 408.52 K. Cone angle has little effect at fixed b (C-14caae5709dc vs C-7105f85b6659).\",\"Geometry failures fit a rule with all 8 failed rows and the valid rows: cos(cone)*(2*b - 0.2) must be below 0.8. For example C-2e989122c857 gives 0.872, which predicts -22 mm against the reported -22.8 mm. C-de1dd6ca3952 gives -716 mm predicted and -715.7 mm reported. At cone 70, b must be at most about 1.24; at cone 68, at most about 1.14; at cone 69, at most about 1.19. I keep all proposals inside this rule with a margin.\",\"C-63aaa0985529 (cone 29.7, b 0.52) and C-62348c286fc5 (cone 40, b 0.5) have bondline temperatures of 409.6 K and 418.35 K. Low bluntness and low cone are clearly worse, so the search should stay at high b and cone.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux falls with larger nose radius (bluntness times D) and lower ballistic coefficient (larger D). Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which is lower for steeper entry and for lower flux. Peak g is set mainly by gamma, with a weak dependence on D. The best design is therefore the largest D that the mass-fraction limit allows (about 3.36-3.38 m), the highest valid bluntness at cone 70 (about 1.2-1.24), and the steepest gamma with g under 12 (about -3.5 to -3.57). Shallower-gamma points at the same geometry add lower-flux, higher-temperature points for front coverage. The D^-1.4 flux scaling and the linear gamma slopes are empirical fits to this data. The soak-time argument is prior physical knowledge.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g dependence on D and b is poorly resolved; D3.25, D3.3 and D3.35 give the same g at gamma -3.5, but D3.1 is lower. Points within 0.02 of g = 12 may fall either way. The mass-fraction coefficient at b > 1.15 is extrapolated, so the D 3.38 probe could go infeasible. The flux and temperature at gamma shallower than -2.6 are extrapolations; the temperature may rise nonlinearly. The b 1.24 and cone 70 geometry sits close to the validity boundary (predicted fore-cone length about 12 mm), so a failure is possible if my fitted rule is slightly off.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Push toward the g and mass limits: D 3.36, higher bluntness 1.2, gamma -3.55, aiming to dominate the incumbent in both objectives.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Most likely candidate to improve hypervolume; tests the joint effect of bluntness, D and gamma near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the previous proposal but gamma -3.5 for more g margin (predicted g about 11.87).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274700.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safe improvement over the incumbent; isolates the bluntness effect at nearly unchanged D and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Higher bluntness 1.24, the geometry-valid maximum at cone 70, with D 3.37 and a shallower gamma of -3.45 for g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269300.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the bluntness gain near the validity boundary and gives a lower-flux front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4f7f664531cd\",\"rationale\":\"Steep gamma -3.56 with D 3.35 and bluntness 1.15 (already known valid) to measure the g and temperature gain from gamma alone.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278900.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.65,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary for large D with a known-valid geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a687c9db7052\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly lower D 3.3 with b 1.2 and steep gamma -3.56; more mass margin and possibly different g behaviour.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283300.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the D effect from the gamma effect on g and temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Mass-fraction probe: D 3.38 with b 1.22 is predicted to have about 0.3% margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271000.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the actual D limit at high b and gives a very low-flux point if feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5b9b5d5a6b\",\"rationale\":\"Combines the highest valid bluntness 1.24 with D 3.36 and gamma -3.53.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272600.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely the best joint candidate; tests the b 1.24 geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a687c9db7052\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 68 and b 1.1 is valid under the geometry rule (0.749 < 0.8). This checks the cone effect at large D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279000.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether cone angle 68 vs 70 matters for flux, temperature and the mass fraction at D 3.36.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma -3.3 at the best geometry to add a lower-flux, slightly warmer point to the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269100.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage along the gamma trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-dc1d6416cb31\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow gamma -3.0 at the large-D, high-b geometry. C-dc1d6416cb31 is the shallow-gamma parent, which was 403 K at D 3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":259800.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the low-flux end of the front and tests the linear gamma slope.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-dc1d6416cb31\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma -2.6 to map the flux-vs-temperature trade-off away from the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248700.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extrapolates the gamma trend and checks for nonlinear soak-time effects.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-dc1d6416cb31\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory shallow gamma -2.2. Flux should drop but temperature should rise.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237700.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the low-flux end of the front becomes worthwhile, or whether temperature rises sharply at shallow entry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma -3.2 for front coverage between -3.0 and -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265300.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the front and refines the gamma slope at large D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-dc1d6416cb31\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate shallow gamma -2.8 at the large-D geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254200.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the response-curve resolution between -2.6 and -3.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9cdb1d4ea87a\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.4 at D 3.36 to get a smooth g and flux response close to the incumbent.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271900.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Confirms the local gradient in gamma at the best geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly smaller D 3.34 with b 1.24 and gamma -3.54; a small D-lowering variation to test how sensitive g is to D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.24,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.54},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275100.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether a slightly smaller D relaxes g enough to allow a steeper gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4f7f664531cd\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69 with b 1.15 (0.753 < 0.8, valid) to check the cone effect at large D and give a mass-fraction data point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.52},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276700.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates cone effects from bluntness effects at the near-optimal D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9cdb1d4ea87a\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.2 at gamma -3.58 to test whether a smaller D permits a steeper gamma at the g limit. Flux is expected to be higher.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":296200.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the D-gamma trade-off at the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-11dcf14fd72e\",\"rationale\":\"Boundary probe: gamma -3.58 at D 3.36 is predicted to be about 12.00 g. If feasible, it gives the lowest bondline temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276900.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390.9,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g = 12 boundary precisely, which is valuable for the remaining rounds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5b9b5d5a6b\",\"rationale\":\"Low-D probe (3.1 m) with gamma -3.62. Lower D should reduce g, allowing a steeper gamma, but flux is higher.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.62},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310800.0,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the D-versus-gamma trade-off for the g constraint at a smaller D and lower mass fraction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":231864,"type":"result","duration_ms":285958,"uuid":"aa133ff5-1f9c-4bce-b62b-5ec1cd231c94","ttft_stream_ms":1150,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1150,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
